Throwing Mjollnir is not necessarily a very bad idea, even in vanilla.
If you have a bag of holding, even a sack, and put all the
rings/wands/potions you're not currently using for something inside,
then Mjollnir can't possibly blow them up. However, I wouldn't highly
reccomend throwing it if you're not a Valkyrie - I've never found Mojo
on a non-Valk, but there's too many spots where you could potentially
lose it - Medusa's level, the trapdoors in the back of the castle
(provided you take that route), the Castle/Fort Ludios moat, some of
the quest levels (including the Valkyrie's if you don't have a BoH and
are throwing to stop the fire ants from destroying your inventory), and
the fake/real Wizard's towers come to mind.

As long as you use it wisely, Mjollnir is perfectly safe to use as your
weapon - provided you don't come across something better first.



